$safetyContent='
<section id="eye-face"><h2>Eye and Face Protection</h2><p>Wear impact-resistant safety glasses where particles or flying objects may be present. Use chemical splash goggles for liquids and a face shield when splash hazards require additional face coverage. Inspect equipment before use and replace damaged items.</p></section>
<section id="hands"><h2>Hand Protection</h2><p>Select gloves based on the chemical, task duration, temperature and mechanical hazard. Check manufacturer compatibility guidance. Remove contaminated gloves by turning them inside out and wash hands after removal.</p></section>
<section id="body"><h2>Body Protection</h2><p>Use appropriate laboratory coats, aprons or coveralls. Close clothing fully, keep sleeves away from equipment, and remove contaminated clothing according to the workplace procedure. Suitable safety footwear protects against impact and spills.</p></section>
<section id="respiratory"><h2>Respiratory Protection</h2><p>Use respiratory equipment only after exposure assessment, fit testing, medical clearance and formal training. Ordinary dust masks are not substitutes for approved respirators. Prefer engineering controls such as local exhaust ventilation.</p></section>
<section id="selection"><h2>PPE Selection Checklist</h2><ul><li>Identify hazards and exposure routes.</li><li>Follow the task risk assessment and safety data sheet.</li><li>Use PPE correctly and inspect it before every task.</li><li>Store, clean and replace PPE according to manufacturer instructions.</li></ul></section>';
